<title>HONG KONG: Deutsche Bank sets warrants on red chips basket.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank sets warrants on red chips basket.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG, London Branch, said on Monday it had launched 1.1 billion American-style warrants on a basket of six red-chip stocks.</p>
<p>Each basket comprises:</p>
<p> China Everbright-IHD Pacific Ltd     0.11 shares</p>
<p> Ng Fung Hong Ltd			   0.08 shares</p>
<p> Guangnan (Holdings) Ltd		  0.08 shares</p>
<p> GZI Transport Ltd			  0.10 shares</p>
<p> China Resources Beijing Land Ltd     0.10 shares</p>
<p> Guangzhou Investment Co Ltd	    0.06 shares</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one basket.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE	HK$3.0834   PREMIUM	   16.50 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	 HK$0.0908   GEARING	   3.8x</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	  02.JAN.98   MIN EXER LOT    10,000</p>
<p> LISTING	     HONG KONG   LISTING DATE    12.MAR.97</p>
<p> SPOT REFERENCE    HK$3.426    PAY DATE	  10.MAR.97</p>
<p> GOVERNING LAW     HONG KONG</p>
<p> NOTE		  CASH OR PHYSICAL DELIVERY AT ISSUER'S OPTION</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
